[28.654,"o","\u001b[1;32mDone. Membrane Materials KB is yours. Next:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[30.254,"o","\r\n"]
[30.474,"o","\u001b[1m  cd membrane-materials-kb\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[31.224,"o","\u001b[1m  uv sync\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[31.974,"o","\u001b[1m  uv run sci-rag doctor\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.724,"o","\u001b[1m  uv run sci-rag draft manifest --folder data/raw\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[33.474,"o","\u001b[1m  uv run sci-rag ingest --manifest data/corpus.jsonl\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.224,"o","\r\n"]
[34.444,"o","Then let a model draft the rest of your domain files:\r\n"]
[34.694,"o","\r\n"]
[34.914,"o","\u001b[1m  uv run sci-rag draft ontology --from-corpus\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[35.664,"o","\u001b[1m  uv run sci-rag draft questions --count 10\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.414,"o","\r\n"]
[36.634,"o","Each one proposes a file for you to review rather than writing one, and each also prints its prompt (--print-prompt) if you would rather paste it into an assistant you already have. Guide: docs/llm-assisted-setup.md\r\n"]
